summary:
The first form is identical to clone_object(). Note that clone_object() is an alias for new().

The second form initializes a struct/class variable, for example:

   class example {
       string name;
       int age;
       string *lover;
   }

   void create()
   {
       // 变量
       class example instance = new(class example);
       // 赋值
       instance->age = 24;
       instance->name = "Ivy";
       instance->lover = ({"Alice", "Vivian", "lucy"});
       // ...
   }

Values can also be supplied directly when initializing a class variable:
       class example instance = new(class example, name:"ivy", age:24, lover:({"Alice","Vivian"}))
